ANNUAL   8760                                      5.69      0.31     4.34

WHAT THIS IS, AND WHAT IT RESTS ON
   hours-weighted annual total-power reduction  : 5.69 %
   hours-weighted annual makeup water reduction : 0.31 %
   hours-weighted annual cost reduction         : 4.34 %

   Those three are means of ratios. As RATIOS OF ANNUAL TOTALS,
   which is what a plant actually banks over a year:
   annual electrical energy reduction           : 4.86 %   (-0.82 pts)
   annual makeup water reduction                : 1.31 %   (+1.00 pts)
   annual operating cost reduction              : 4.01 %   (-0.33 pts)
   The energy and water corrections have OPPOSITE signs.
   for comparison, the five-condition unweighted mean the V5 gate
   scores                                        : 4.38 % water

   fraction of the year INSIDE the validated wet-bulb envelope
   (<= 21.9 C), counted hour by hour           : 59.5 %
   fraction resting on EXTRAPOLATION            : 40.5 %   (3551 h)

   AND WHAT THE EXTRAPOLATION IS ACTUALLY WORTH -- defects 48 and 60.

                                   hours   water %  energy %   cost %
   whole year                       8760      1.31      4.86     4.01
   inside the validated envelope    5209     -3.22      8.82     5.32
   EXTRAPOLATED (wb > 21.9 C)       3551      5.41      0.95     2.75

   The water saving is NEGATIVE inside the validated wet-bulb envelope and positive only outside it, so the annual water figure is carried entirely by extrapolated hours.
   The energy saving is the reverse: larger inside the envelope than outside it.
   Quote neither without this split.

   Roughly two fifths of this TMYx year is hotter and wetter than
   anything the model was validated against, and no amount of
   weighting changes that. It is what the KFUPM wind tunnel is for.
   How much of that fraction is the TMYx file's humidity rather than
   Dhahran's is docs/weather_source_sensitivity.md.

